Package: netmatchRI
Title: Network-Constrained Matching and Randomization-Based Inference
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Zhejia", "Dong", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    email = "zhejia_dong@brown.edu")
Author: Zhejia Dong [aut, cre]
Maintainer: Zhejia Dong <zhejia_dong@brown.edu>
Description: Provides network-constrained matching and randomization-based
    inference for observational network data with dependence and interference.
    The three matching methods are dual-penalty, single-penalty, and
    covariate-only matching. Dual-penalty matching balances covariates while
    enforcing network-distance restrictions between treatment arms and within
    matched sets. The package also provides diagnostics for covariate balance
    and network distance, design-based covariance bounds, sensitivity analysis,
    and simulated network data. The open-source 'HiGHS' solver is used by
    default to obtain the optimal matching design.
    An optional interface to the commercial 'Gurobi Optimizer' is available.
    Eligible academic users can request a free license at
    <https://www.gurobi.com/academics/>. The optimizer can be downloaded from
    <https://www.gurobi.com/product/download-center>. The associated 'gurobi'
    R package is not available from CRAN; it is distributed with the optimizer
    and can be installed by following the official instructions at
    <https://docs.gurobi.com/projects/optimizer/en/current/reference/r/setup.html>.
